 "comments": [
  {
   "id": "e18d474a-e745-4875-96e0-bbda74ff677d",
   "build_id": "42369f7d-6a9b-45a2-a284-892ee8d5e70d",
   "author_id": "d1cfb49c-81ec-4090-b56e-16fc4df92f17",
   "parent_id": null,
   "body": "First of all, excellent build.  Highly recommend it to anyone interested in learning tanking. My personal recommendation for pulling is to basically just spam bow and arrow everywhere.  Alongside Shooting Star/Huntress Saber to get out in front of the group, I typically didn't have many issues keeping aggro.  Snap threat is definitely Moon Guard's biggest issue though; I regularly would lose 1 or 2 mobs in the pile-up because I couldn't click on their tags.  Also, if you don't get back your Starburst between crowd pulls, Starshatter can be an excellent alternative.\n\n2nd, I REALLY underestimated how insane Coalesced Resilience is.  It is, without question, Moon Guard's best talent.  I typically have around 8-10k mana, which means it's a flat reduction of 80-100 damage on every swipe.  I went from pulling 2-3 packs to literally pulling everything and the boss after.  Even damage that was chunking before it turned into minor inconveniences.  I'm sure it'll scale less optimally into Heroic and Mythic dungeons compared to percentage reductions, but in standard dungeons it's an insane talent.",
   "upvotes": 1,
